{"_v":1,"id":"the-color-purple-2005","cat":"broadway","cs":72.56,"rc":6,"bd":{"positive":3,"mixed":3,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Alissa Wilkinson","o":"The New York Times","s":76,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.nytimes.com/2007/05/18/theater/reviews/18purp.html","d":"2007-05-18","q":"“The Color Purple” has been born again, and its conversion is a glory to behold."},{"cn":"Charles Isherwood","o":"Variety","s":66,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://variety.com/2005/legit/reviews/the-color-purple-1200524646/","d":"2005-12-02","q":"Like everything else in the show, the musical elements are a far-from-seamless mix, alternating flat stretches with stirring peaks, and too many songs feel incomplete."},{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"The New York Times","s":63,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.nytimes.com/2005/12/02/theater/02purp.html","d":"2005-12-02","q":"But it never slows down long enough for you to embrace it."},{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"About Entertainment","s":62,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"http://theater.nytimes.com/2005/12/02/theater/reviews/02purp.html","d":"2005-12-02","q":"As for the rest of the production, there's a sumptuousness throughout that, while hardly true to the harrowing bleakness of the early chapters of Ms. Walker's novel, does bring to mind the enjoyably hokey cinematic ravishments of Steven Spielberg's 1985 film version."},{"cn":"Eric March","o":"Theater Life","s":92,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://theaterlife.com/the-color-purple/","d":"2007-01-18","q":"Making an impressive Broadway debut director Gary Griffin has turned The Color Purple into a glorious rarity, a pure life affirming entertainment that is a thrill to behold."},{"cn":"Matthew Murray","o":"Talkin' Broadway","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.talkinbroadway.com/page/regional/boston/b530.html","d":"2005-12-12"}],"au":{"score":78,"designation":"Liking","sources":{"mz":{"s":78,"c":52,"sr":3.9}}},"tn":[{"yr":60,"cat":"Best Actress in a Musical","n":"LaChanze","w":true},{"yr":60,"cat":"Bes